shell: ask for no depth or stencil buffer in the shell windows

Every Qt Quick window asks EGL for depth 24 + stencil 8 (Qt 6.10
qsgdefaultcontext.cpp), so Mesa keeps a window-size depth-stencil
buffer per shell window. The shell draws flat 2D layers, so set
QSG_NO_DEPTH_BUFFER and QSG_NO_STENCIL_BUFFER for the shell process.
(J604 build: the shell.qml hunk of up/kits/g1qsds/shell-f97-qsds.patch,
the change K-G1-QSDS measures.)

diff --git a/shell/shell.qml b/shell/shell.qml
--- a/shell/shell.qml
+++ b/shell/shell.qml
@@ -1,4 +1,6 @@
 //@ pragma OmarchyLoadPatch
+//@ pragma Env QSG_NO_DEPTH_BUFFER = 1
+//@ pragma Env QSG_NO_STENCIL_BUFFER = 1
 import QtQuick
 import QtQml.Models
 import Quickshell
